# cabin_sky_clear: the clear sky over the cabin (BUILD_PLAN S7), the whole
# sky layer, placed at the plate's origin by web/js/gfx/cabin.js: glacier
# blue, flat, from the very top through the name (rows 0 to 28 stay clean,
# lead call 61) down to the peak's summit, then a horizon band fourteen rows
# deep, a checker25 seam into a checker seam into solid snow: the hour's
# table makes it slate over a real pink glow at dusk and dawn, slate over
# glacier at blue hour, navy over slate at night (so the name's night sky
# is navy, dark and blue, 6.3), and a pale haze by day. It shows in the gaps
# by the peak and the spruce; it starts under the summit, so the snowy crest
# stands on clear glacier blue at every hour. Its frame runs one pixel
# outside the plate, so no band's fill reaches the stamp's edge; the plate
# clips it.
C 9  L -1,-1 160,-1 160,171 -1,171 -1,-1
# The horizon's glow, cut by ink rows; each band's fill takes its row too.
C 0  L 0,54 159,54  L 0,59 159,59  L 0,64 159,64
C 3              F 80,30
D 3 4 checker25  F 80,56 80,54
D 3 4 checker    F 80,61 80,59
C 4              F 80,120 80,64
